      "ownership_changed": false,
      "node_id": "node:2d20d031463e78b93c69729a0ce0aa48f5d62585d7183459ba8938412f3320ca",
      "occurrence_id": "node:86a4cddf55b0cea96a9b9b732ee1296274a43669dd7d5e5aaec6cc13aa50af36",
      "span": {
        "source_id": "source:90174b7b21484936f3c0dfe0161b4aec387dcc47cdbac4a8122d5151fc032ef8",
        "source_sha256": "sha256:5f49b0a77834ac5184f6b52e9d06e9380a6b88a3e0f428f5381aecba9678382e",
        "path": "ORIGINAL-0001.txt",
        "char_start": 1522,
        "char_end": 1952,
        "byte_start": 1524,
        "byte_end": 1954,
        "text": "\nAlmost immediately after France fell to the Nazis in 1940, the Allies planned a cross-Channel assault on the German occupying forces. At the Quebec Conference in August 1943, Winston Churchill and Franklin Roosevelt reaffirmed the plan, which was code-named Overlord. Although Churchill acceded begrudgingly to the operation, historians note that the British still harbored persistent doubts about whether Overlord would succeed."
      },
